github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/pull/6204#issuecomment-5534363524","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUMmgW88AAAABSd_JLQ","author":{"login":"qodo-code-review"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"<h3>Code Review by Qodo</h3>\n\n<code>🐞 Bugs (1)</code>  <code>📘 Rule violations (0)</code>  <code>📜 Skill insights (0)</code>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n<br/>\n\n<img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/High-634FD1?style=flat-square\" height=\"20px\" alt=\"Action required\">\n\n<details>\n<summary>  1.  Explicit env loses precedence <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>≡ Correctness</code></summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Description</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n><b><i>load_dotenv</i></b> now merges the explicit file before the defaults, so later <b><i>.flaskenv</i></b> or <b><i>.env</i></b>\n>entries overwrite duplicate keys from <b><i>--env-file</i></b>. This violates the CLI&#x27;s documented precedence\n>and can start an application with incorrect configuration.\n></pre>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Code</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><code>[src/flask/cli.py[R745-746]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/pull/6204/files#diff-fed8939d1905b99bba605ad91e9ccdf5ede6223e03ccbc3f0121853035051e62R745-R746)</code>\n>\n>```diff\n>+    if path is not None and os.path.isfile(path):\n>+        data |= dotenv.dotenv_values(path, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n>```\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>The explicit path is merged at lines 745-746, while default files are merged afterward at lines\n>748-753 using dictionary update semantics, replacing duplicate keys. The option and class\n>documentation explicitly promise that <b><i>-e/--env-file</i></b> takes precedence, and the callback invokes\n><b><i>load_dotenv</i></b> with both the explicit path and default loading enabled.\n></pre>\n>\n> <code>[src/flask/cli.py[745-759]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/blob/2ceb4fb3ac91432a2c43cdcd28d9b61d37244a4a/src/flask/cli.py/#L745-L759)</code>\n> <code>[src/flask/cli.py[508-523]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/blob/2ceb4fb3ac91432a2c43cdcd28d9b61d37244a4a/src/flask/cli.py/#L508-L523)</code>\n> <code>[src/flask/cli.py[548-550]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/blob/2ceb4fb3ac91432a2c43cdcd28d9b61d37244a4a/src/flask/cli.py/#L548-L550)</code>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n>```\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\n>\n>## Issue description\n>`load_dotenv` loads the explicit path before default files, allowing `.flaskenv` and `.env` to overwrite explicitly supplied values.\n>\n>## Issue Context\n>The `--env-file` option documents that its values take precedence over both default files, while directly supplied process environment variables retain highest precedence.\n>\n>## Fix Focus Areas\n>- src/flask/cli.py[743-759]\n>- tests/test_cli.py[535-566]\n>```\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n></details>\n\n<hr/>\n</details>\n\n\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n\n<!-- qodo-context:start -->\n<details><summary><strong>Context sources</strong></summary>\n\n<div>Review mode: <code>⚖️ Balanced</code>: This is a small but behavior-changing environment-loading-order update in Flask CLI code, so compatibility and edge-case review warrant a careful single pass.</div>\n<!-- qodo-context:end -->\n</details>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n\n\n<!-- qodo-daily-tip:start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Tip of the day</strong></summary>\n\n<br/>\n